{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0FFJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{1}$", "MATH_0002": "$1 : \\mathbf{1} \\otimes \\mathbf{1} \\to \\mathbf{1}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathbf{1}, 1)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-monoidal-unit-unique}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67dbc7e47beebb9906cee0ee6e8805a98079bffb1daa9a7268c73f0ac6a74551", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f4fc2d9ee6d623f488ca2c7ca1af5e27d1a63dc3d04a4defb0850dd74c16e3a1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe always write <MATH_0001> to denote a unit of a monoidal category\nand we denote <MATH_0002>\na chosen isomorphism; as the pair <MATH_0003> is determined\nup to unique isomorphism (Lemma <REF_0001>)\nthere is no harm in choosing one.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6f3d065fe00963e0f06660088238a9602d617a3819782c66d1ae395234fa4e46", "unit_id": "tag:0FFJ:prose-0002"}
